    {
      "id": "demo-04",
      "group": "a. docs/DEMO.md, map mode",
      "mode": "map",
      "question": "What are the rules for the active floodplain?",
      "point_name": "P_ZONEO",
      "lat": 28.672913,
      "lon": 77.243545,
      "expect": "answer",
      "note": "beat 3, sharper",
      "ran_at": "2026-10-20T05:16:02+00:00",
      "error": null,
      "zones_text": "planning zone O; in Zone O (Yamuna floodplain)",
      "located_lat": 28.672913,
      "located_lon": 77.243545,
      "answer": "The active floodplain is designated as a ‘no construction zone’ where only recreational uses are permitted and any unauthorised construction, including religious structures, must be demolished by the concerned agency on priority [C1].\nEssential government utilities, socio‑cultural and recreational activities, public infrastructure development and conservation of floodplains are allowed only with the approval or NOC of the competent authority or statutory body [C1].\nAreas outside the active floodplain are subject to restricted development; existing authorised and planned constructions and essential government utilities may continue as per permissible norms and with approval or NOC, while further development is limited to socio‑cultural, recreational uses, essential utilities and public infrastructure with the same approvals [C1].",
      "answer_words": 112,
      "citations": [
        {
